{
  "id": "80623",
  "type": "Page",
  "tags": [],
  "title": "Cell Notation",
  "content": {
    "bibrefs": [],
    "model": [
      {
        "children": [
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "text": "Chemists often use a compact notation to efficiently describe the composition of electrochemical cells. This "
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "cell notation"
                  }
                ],
                "content": [
                  {
                    "children": [
                      {
                        "text": "A symbolic representation of the components and reactions in an electrochemical cell; also called "
                      },
                      {
                        "em": true,
                        "text": "cell diagram"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "."
                      }
                    ],
                    "id": "814262621",
                    "type": "p"
                  }
                ],
                "id": "2710364812",
                "trigger": "hover",
                "type": "popup"
              },
              {
                "text": " (also called a "
              },
              {
                "em": true,
                "text": "cell diagram"
              },
              {
                "text": ") provides information about the species involved in the reaction and how the cell is constructed. In this representation:"
              }
            ],
            "id": "aczeqnfami37oe4",
            "type": "p"
          },
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "children": [
                      {
                        "text": "Species involved in the oxidation half-reaction are written on the left, and species in the reduction half-reaction are on the right."
                      }
                    ],
                    "id": "2161803694",
                    "type": "p"
                  }
                ],
                "id": "deccmxk7cqpn8pd",
                "type": "li"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "children": [
                      {
                        "text": "The anode is written farthest to the left and the cathode is written farthest to the right."
                      }
                    ],
                    "id": "698639997",
                    "type": "p"
                  }
                ],
                "id": "80q0h442cwqw8fx",
                "type": "li"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "children": [
                      {
                        "text": "A vertical line, │, denotes a phase boundary and a double line, ║, indicates the salt bridge (and separates the two half-reactions)."
                      }
                    ],
                    "id": "622379382",
                    "type": "p"
                  }
                ],
                "id": "epcuh0vfowwd5c6",
                "type": "li"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "children": [
                      {
                        "text": "If reactants and products of a half-reaction are in the same phase, we use a comma to separate them."
                      }
                    ],
                    "id": "2839726453",
                    "type": "p"
                  }
                ],
                "id": "f60iqa4k02kfjsn",
                "type": "li"
              }
            ],
            "id": "6lpxw3oi55omk6z",
            "type": "ul"
          },
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "text": "The cell notation for the galvanic cell described on the previous page is shown here:"
              }
            ],
            "id": "cdyuqdvnooy7aru",
            "type": "p"
          },
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "id": "r777hq5mfpmilju",
                "text": " ",
                "type": "text"
              }
            ],
            "id": "z085gcjlmbdc9fs",
            "legacyBlockRendered": "true",
            "src": "\\mathrm{Cu}(s)│\\mathrm{Cu}^{2+}(aq,\\;1\\;\\mathrm M)║\\mathrm{Ag}^+(aq,\\;1\\;\\mathrm M)│\\mathrm{Ag}(s)",
            "subtype": "latex",
            "type": "formula"
          },
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "id": "tkele80uonpy595",
                "text": " ",
                "type": "text"
              }
            ],
            "id": "rlwe1i4uhpymx0t",
            "src": "https://d2xvti2irp4c7t.cloudfront.net/media/3f/3fd138194a6af429fc860bca87260448/cell_notation.png",
            "type": "img",
            "width": "600"
          },
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "text": ""
              }
            ],
            "id": "2608515119",
            "type": "p"
          }
        ],
        "id": "2140619919",
        "selection": {
          "anchor": {
            "offset": 0,
            "path": [
              0,
              0
            ]
          },
          "focus": {
            "offset": 0,
            "path": [
              1,
              0
            ]
          }
        },
        "type": "content"
      },
      {
        "children": [
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "Consider a galvanic cell that uses the reaction:"
                  }
                ],
                "id": "sgqi8cykwsi61vv",
                "type": "p"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "id": "86ridkwr9vlxfdt",
                    "text": " ",
                    "type": "text"
                  }
                ],
                "id": "6om1bij7li38d9z",
                "legacyBlockRendered": "true",
                "src": "2\\;\\mathrm{Cr}(s)\\;+\\;3\\;\\mathrm{Cu}^{2+}(aq)\\;\\;\\longrightarrow\\;\\;2\\;\\mathrm{Cr}^{3+}(aq)\\; +\\;3\\;\\mathrm{Cu}(s)",
                "subtype": "latex",
                "type": "formula"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "Write the oxidation and reduction half-reactions. Which reaction occurs at the anode? Which occurs at the cathode? Write the shorthand notation for this galvanic cell."
                  }
                ],
                "id": "kicqkwcxll9d8g9",
                "type": "p"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "By inspection, Cr is oxidized when three electrons are lost to form Cr"
                  },
                  {
                    "sup": true,
                    "text": "3+"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ", and Cu"
                  },
                  {
                    "sup": true,
                    "text": "2+"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " is reduced as it gains two electrons to form Cu. Balancing the charge gives:"
                  }
                ],
                "id": "lqxc16au995ph5l",
                "type": "p"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "id": "6wgb5zpeatt7ums",
                    "text": " ",
                    "type": "text"
                  }
                ],
                "id": "wfykyy76s2k1l01",
                "legacyBlockRendered": "true",
                "src": "\\begin{array}{l}\\mathrm{Oxidation}:\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;2\\;\\mathrm{Cr}(s) \\;\\longrightarrow\\;2\\;\\mathrm{Cr}^{3+}(aq)\\;+\\;6\\;\\mathrm e^-\\\\\\underline{\\mathrm{Reduction}:\\;\\;\\; 3\\;\\mathrm{Cu}^{2+}(aq)\\;+\\;6\\;\\mathrm e^-\\;\\;\\longrightarrow\\;\\;3\\;\\mathrm{Cu}(s)\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\; \\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;}\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\; \\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\\\\\mathrm{Overall}:\\;\\;\\;\\;2\\;\\mathrm{Cr}(s)\\;+\\;3\\; \\mathrm{Cu}^{2+}(aq)\\;\\;\\longrightarrow\\;\\;2\\;\\mathrm{Cr}^{3+}(aq)\\;+\\;3\\;\\mathrm{Cu}(s)\\end{array}",
                "subtype": "latex",
                "type": "formula"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "We start on the left with information about the oxidation half-reaction. The anode, Cr("
                  },
                  {
                    "em": true,
                    "text": "s"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "), is written farthest to the left. Next is a single line, │, representing the phase boundary, followed by the Cr"
                  },
                  {
                    "sup": true,
                    "text": "3+"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "("
                  },
                  {
                    "em": true,
                    "text": "aq"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ") ions in the solution."
                  }
                ],
                "id": "2echkfvzvdbvr80",
                "type": "p"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "Next, we write a double line, ║, to indicate the salt bridge and separate the two half-reactions."
                  }
                ],
                "id": "ee3arj8yvpzu0gc",
                "type": "p"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "Finally, we state the information about the reduction half-reaction. First, we write the Cu"
                  },
                  {
                    "sup": true,
                    "text": "2+"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "("
                  },
                  {
                    "em": true,
                    "text": "aq"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ") ions in the solution. Next is a single line, │, representing the phase boundary. The cathode, Cu("
                  },
                  {
                    "em": true,
                    "text": "s"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "), is written farthest to the right."
                  }
                ],
                "id": "a3mudjyv3zjp1de",
                "type": "p"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "The cell notation is therefore:"
                  }
                ],
                "id": "8ju4uha1wr36a1k",
                "type": "p"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "id": "71jur9vks9e7pdn",
                    "text": " ",
                    "type": "text"
                  }
                ],
                "id": "lnuh51lwuynwte1",
                "legacyBlockRendered": "true",
                "src": "\\mathrm{Cr}(s)│\\mathrm{Cr}^{3+}(aq)║\\mathrm{Cu}^{2+}(aq)│\\mathrm{Cu}(s)",
                "subtype": "latex",
                "type": "formula"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "Note that this notation provides information about the reactants and products of the redox reaction that occurs in the cell, but it does not explicitly state the stoichiometric coefficients for the reaction. (These coefficients can be determined relatively easily from the information given in the cell notation.)"
                  }
                ],
                "id": "js3vtzoocgffqd5",
                "type": "p"
              }
            ],
            "id": "1043036824",
            "selection": {
              "anchor": {
                "offset": 0,
                "path": [
                  0,
                  0
                ]
              },
              "focus": {
                "offset": 0,
                "path": [
                  1,
                  0
                ]
              }
            },
            "type": "content"
          }
        ],
        "id": "2700210844",
        "layout": "vertical",
        "purpose": "example",
        "type": "group"
      },
      {
        "children": [
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "Use the following description of a galvanic cell to answer the questions that follow."
                  }
                ],
                "id": "100jzahm0o5uq5n",
                "type": "p"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "One half-cell consists of a gold electrode in a 1.0 M Au(NO"
                  },
                  {
                    "sub": true,
                    "text": "3"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ")"
                  },
                  {
                    "sub": true,
                    "text": "3"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " solution, and the other half-cell is a magnesium electrode in a 1.0 M Mg(NO"
                  },
                  {
                    "sub": true,
                    "text": "3"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ")"
                  },
                  {
                    "sub": true,
                    "text": "2"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " solution. The salt bridge contains NaNO"
                  },
                  {
                    "sub": true,
                    "text": "3"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ". NO"
                  },
                  {
                    "sub": true,
                    "text": "3"
                  },
                  {
                    "sup": true,
                    "text": "−"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ions from the salt bridge flow toward the cell containing the Mg(NO"
                  },
                  {
                    "sub": true,
                    "text": "3"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ")"
                  },
                  {
                    "sub": true,
                    "text": "2"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " solution, and Na"
                  },
                  {
                    "sup": true,
                    "text": "+"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ions flow toward the cell containing the Au(NO"
                  },
                  {
                    "sub": true,
                    "text": "3"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ")"
                  },
                  {
                    "sub": true,
                    "text": "3"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " solution."
                  }
                ],
                "id": "i7mhsrphzsv8cha",
                "type": "p"
              }
            ],
            "id": "4265209726",
            "selection": {
              "anchor": {
                "offset": 0,
                "path": [
                  0,
                  0
                ]
              },
              "focus": {
                "offset": 0,
                "path": [
                  1,
